      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 874670667,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "setCurrentIndex should already do that. If it is not working, we should reconsider the mechanics behind that, as it is used more often.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-03-15T06:46:30.706Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-03-15T06:46:30.706Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 144974679,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 6433,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 874855698,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "There is something else to consider as well. setCurrentIndex will lead to Signals being fired. If anything, the change should catch that signal, question if the selected Item is visible and then elect to fire \"gotoPacket\" if that is not the case. We have 10 places in PacketList alone, which set the current index, this would only handle a single potential case.\n\nAlso, this is not a change to the original issue. The original issue stated, that changing the packet comment does not update after a change. So the issue here is not reselecting the packet, but instead make ProtoTree aware, that the content of the packet has changed and therefore it needs to update its content. Same goes for any other subview in the future.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-03-15T09:18:33.421Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-03-15T09:18:33.421Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 144974679,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 6433,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "730f15b989c92a12b1e617c9fd0a5146bf79b51a",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 874918586,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The reason why this issue is being raised in the first place is the fact, that the original changes ignored the Model/View concept and implemented the comments in a separate way. If it would have been implemented within PacketListModel (where it belongs) the correct signals would propagate and the ProtoTree would have been updated automatically and had been informed of the change. Also, there is now a lot of specific code in MainWindow, which does not belong there (aka, firing updates which in itself is a circumvention of signal/slot). There will be other places that did not get the information about the comments, because of that. \n\nThe PacketCommentDialog on the other hand, breaks the Qt Widget concept, by not adhering to the proper setup for dialogs (QWidget parent being first) and has no correlation with the packet in question (it basically is just a simple text control). The dialog should save the value to the model, by simply referencing the selected index, which in turn would lead to a lot of code in MainWindow being obsolete. \n\nBasically, we dropped the ball on this one.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-03-15T10:00:38.804Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-03-15T10:00:38.804Z",
